### Design notes

| Decision | Rationale |
|---|---|
| `Object.create(null)` | Avoids prototype pollution and collisions with keys like `"toString"` or `"__proto__"`. |
| Single pass with `forEach` | O(n), easy to read, and avoids the allocation overhead of `reduce` with spread patterns. |
| Index passed to `keyFn` | Enables positional grouping (chunking, alternating) at no extra cost. |
| Input validation | Fails fast with clear messages instead of obscure runtime errors. |
| Separate `Map` variant | Object keys are always strings or symbols. `Map` preserves key identity when that matters. |
| Stable ordering | Elements in each group keep their original order, which makes output predictable and testable. |

