## Design Notes

| Decision | Rationale |
|---|---|
| **`Object.create(null)`** | Prevents bugs when a key is `"__proto__"`, `"toString"`, `"hasOwnProperty"`, etc. |
| **Single `for` loop** | O(n), no intermediate arrays. Faster than chaining `reduce` with spreads, which can become O(n²). |
| **Passes `(item, index, array)`** | Matches the familiar `Array.prototype.map/filter` callback signature. |
| **Runtime type checks** | Gives clear error messages for JS callers who don't have type checking. |
| **Separate `Map` variant** | Plain objects coerce keys to strings and reorder integer-like keys. `Map` avoids both. |

> **Note:** Modern runtimes (ES2024+, Node 21+) include the built-ins `Object.groupBy(arr, fn)` and `Map.groupBy(arr, fn)`, which behave like the two functions above. If your target environment supports them, prefer the built-ins. This utility is useful as a polyfill or for older environments.

