## Design Notes

| Decision | Rationale |
|---|---|
| **Null-prototype result object** | Prevents keys like `"constructor"` or `"__proto__"` from colliding with or polluting `Object.prototype`. |
| **`keyFn` receives `(item, index, array)`** | Matches familiar array callback conventions and enables index-based grouping (e.g. chunking). |
| **Stable ordering** | Elements keep their original relative order inside each group, which makes results predictable. |
| **Separate `Map` variant** | Plain objects stringify keys, so `1` and `"1"` merge. `groupByToMap` preserves key identity and supports object keys. |
| **Runtime type checks** | Gives clear error messages for JavaScript callers who don't get compile-time checks. |

> **Note:** Modern runtimes (ES2024+: Node 21+, Chrome 117+, Safari 17.4+) ship a native [`Object.groupBy`](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Object/groupBy) and `Map.groupBy` with nearly identical semantics. If your target environments support them, prefer the built-ins. This utility is useful as a polyfill or when you need to support older environments.

