## Design notes

| Decision | Rationale |
|---|---|
| **Only transient statuses retried** | A `404` or `401` won't fix itself, so retrying just wastes time and load. |
| **Full jitter** | Prevents many clients from retrying in lockstep after an outage (the "thundering herd" problem). |
| **`Retry-After` honored** | Servers that rate-limit (429) often say exactly when to come back. |
| **Last response returned, not thrown** | Preserves native `fetch` behavior, so callers still check `res.ok`. |
| **Caller abort respected** | Cancelling stops retries immediately, including mid-backoff. |
| **Per-attempt timeout** | A hung connection counts as a failure and gets retried, instead of hanging forever. |
| **`retries` accepts number or object** | Keeps the simple `(url, options, 3)` signature while allowing full configuration. |

