**Design notes**

- **Exponential backoff with full jitter:** delays grow as 500ms, 1s, 2s, 4s… (capped), randomized so many clients don't retry in lockstep.
- **Smart retry decisions:** only transient failures (network errors, 408/429/5xx) are retried; client errors return immediately.
- **`Retry-After` support:** respects server rate-limit guidance.
- **Abort-friendly:** an `AbortSignal` stops retries immediately.
- **Behavior on exhaustion:** returns the final retryable response (so you can inspect status/body) or throws the final network error.

