 *   - onRetry {Function}: callback invoked before each wait (useful for logging)
 *   - signal {AbortSignal}: aborting cancels the request and any pending wait
 * @param {number} [retries=3] - Maximum number of retries (total attempts = retries + 1).
 * @returns {Promise<Response>} Resolves with the first non-retryable response.
 *   If retries are exhausted on a retryable HTTP status, the last Response is
 *   returned so the caller can inspect it.
 * @throws {Error} The last network error if all attempts fail with exceptions,
 *   or an AbortError if the request is aborted.
 *
 * @example
 * const res = await fetchWithRetry(
 *   "https://api.example.com/data",
 *   { method: "GET", baseDelay: 300, onRetry: ({attempt, delay}) =>
 *       console.log(`Retry #${attempt} in ${delay}ms`) },
 *   5
 * );
 * if (!res.ok) throw new Error(`HTTP ${res.status}`);
 * const data = await res.json();
