```js
/** A small in-memory cache with no expiration or eviction. */
class Cache {
  #entries = new Map();

  /** Returns the value for `key`, or undefined if the key is absent. */
  get(key) {
    return this.#entries.get(key);
  }

  /** Stores `value` at `key`, replacing any existing value. Returns this cache. */
  set(key, value) {
    this.#entries.set(key, value);
    return this;
  }

  /** Returns true if `key` exists, even if its value is undefined. */
  has(key) {
    return this.#entries.has(key);
  }

  /** Removes `key`. Returns true if an entry was removed, or false otherwise. */
  delete(key) {
    return this.#entries.delete(key);
  }
}
```

Keys and values can be any JavaScript value. Use `has(key)` to distinguish a missing key from one that stores `undefined`.

