The implementation delegates to a private `Map`, so keys can be any Map-compatible key (strings, numbers, objects), and iteration methods (`keys()`, `size`, etc.) are easy to add later if needed.

# Cache

A simple in-memory key/value cache with optional per-entry expiration.

## Public API

### `new Cache()`
Creates a new, empty cache instance.

### `get(key) → value | undefined`
Returns the cached value for `key`, or `undefined` if the key is absent or its entry has expired. Reading an expired entry removes it.

### `set(key, value, [ttlMs]) → this`
Stores `value` under `key`. If `ttlMs` (milliseconds) is provided, the entry expires after that duration. Returns the cache for chaining.

### `has(key) → boolean`
Returns `true` if `key` exists and has not expired. Does not return the value.

### `delete(key) → boolean`
Removes `key` from the cache. Returns `true` if the key existed, `false` otherwise.

---

## Implementation

```js
class Cache {
  #entries = new Map(); // key -> { value, expiresAt }

  #isExpired(entry) {
    return entry.expiresAt !== undefined && Date.now() > entry.expiresAt;
  }

  /**
   * Get the value for `key`, or undefined if missing/expired.
   * @param {*} key
   * @returns {*|undefined}
   */
  get(key) {
    const entry = this.#entries.get(key);
    if (!entry) return undefined;
    if (this.#isExpired(entry)) {
      this.#entries.delete(key);
      return undefined;
    }
    return entry.value;
  }

  /**
   * Store `value` under `key`, optionally expiring after `ttlMs` milliseconds.
   * @param {*} key
   * @param {*} value
   * @param {number} [ttlMs] - time-to-live in milliseconds
   * @returns {Cache} this (for chaining)
   */
  set(key, value, ttlMs) {
    const expiresAt = ttlMs === undefined ? undefined : Date.now() + ttlMs;
    this.#entries.set(key, { value, expiresAt });
    return this;
  }

  /**
   * Check whether `key` exists and is not expired.
   * @param {*} key
   * @returns {boolean}
   */
  has(key) {
    const entry = this.#entries.get(key);
    if (!entry) return false;
    if (this.#isExpired(entry)) {
      this.#entries.delete(key);
      return false;
    }
    return true;
  }

  /**
   * Remove `key` from the cache.
   * @param {*} key
   * @returns {boolean} true if the key existed
   */
  delete(key) {
    return this.#entries.delete(key);
  }
}
```

## Usage

```js
const cache = new Cache();

cache.set("user:1", { name: "Ada" }, 60_000); // expires in 60s

cache.has("user:1");   // true
cache.get("user:1");   // { name: "Ada" }
cache.delete("user:1"); // true
cache.has("user:1");   // false
```

**Notes:**
- Keys can be any value usable as a `Map` key (objects included, compared by identity).
- Expiration is checked lazily on access; no timers run in the background.
- `get` returning `undefined` is ambiguous between "missing" and "stored `undefined`" — use `has` if you need to distinguish those cases.

# Cache Class

A small in-memory cache with optional capacity limit (LRU eviction).

```js
/**
 * Cache — a simple in-memory key/value cache.
 */
class Cache {
  /**
   * @param {number} [maxSize=Infinity] - Max entries before oldest are evicted.
   */
  constructor(maxSize = Infinity) {
    this._maxSize = maxSize;
    this._store = new Map(); // Map preserves insertion order (used for LRU)
  }

  /**
   * Get a value by key. Returns undefined if not found.
   * Refreshes the key as "most recently used".
   * @param {*} key
   * @returns {*|undefined}
   */
  get(key) {
    if (!this._store.has(key)) return undefined;
    const value = this._store.get(key);
    this._store.delete(key);
    this._store.set(key, value); // move to end (most recent)
    return value;
  }

  /**
   * Set a value for a key. Evicts oldest entry if over capacity.
   * @param {*} key
   * @param {*} value
   * @returns {void}
   */
  set(key, value) {
    if (this._store.has(key)) this._store.delete(key);
    this._store.set(key, value);
    if (this._store.size > this._maxSize) {
      this._store.delete(this._store.keys().next().value); // evict oldest
    }
  }

  /**
   * Check whether a key exists (does NOT refresh recency).
   * @param {*} key
   * @returns {boolean}
   */
  has(key) {
    return this._store.has(key);
  }

  /**
   * Delete a key. Returns true if the key existed.
   * @param {*} key
   * @returns {boolean}
   */
  delete(key) {
    return this._store.delete(key);
  }

  /** Number of entries currently cached. */
  get size() {
    return this._store.size;
  }
}
```

## Public API

| Method | Description |
|---|---|
| `new Cache(maxSize?)` | Create a cache. `maxSize` limits entries (default: unlimited). |
| `get(key)` | Return the value (or `undefined` if missing). Marks the key as recently used. |
| `set(key, value)` | Store/overwrite a value; evicts least-recently-used entry when over capacity. |
| `has(key)` | Return `true` if the key exists. |
| `delete(key)` | Remove a key; returns `true` if it existed. |
| `size` | Getter for the current number of entries. |

## Example

```js
const cache = new Cache(2);
cache.set("a", 1);
cache.set("b", 2);
cache.get("a");      // 1  ("a" is now most recent)
cache.set("c", 3);   // evicts "b"
cache.has("b");      // false
cache.delete("a");   // true
```

# Cache Class

A simple in-memory key-value cache with a maximum size and LRU-style eviction (least recently used entries are removed first).

## Usage

```javascript
const cache = new Cache({ maxSize: 100 });

cache.set("user:1", { name: "Alice" });
cache.has("user:1");   // true
cache.get("user:1");   // { name: "Alice" }
cache.delete("user:1"); // true
cache.get("user:1");   // undefined
```

## Implementation

```javascript
/**
 * A simple in-memory cache with a maximum size.
 * When the cache is full, the least recently used entry is evicted.
 */
class Cache {
  /**
   * @param {Object} [options]
   * @param {number} [options.maxSize=100] - Maximum number of entries.
   *   Must be a positive integer.
   * @throws {TypeError} If maxSize is not a positive integer.
   */
  constructor({ maxSize = 100 } = {}) {
    if (!Number.isInteger(maxSize) || maxSize <= 0) {
      throw new TypeError("maxSize must be a positive integer");
    }
    this._maxSize = maxSize;
    /** @type {Map<any, any>} Insertion-ordered; last entry = most recently used. */
    this._store = new Map();
  }

  /**
   * Retrieve a value from the cache.
   * Marks the entry as most recently used.
   *
   * @param {*} key - The key to look up.
   * @returns {*} The cached value, or `undefined` if the key is not present.
   */
  get(key) {
    if (!this._store.has(key)) return undefined;
    const value = this._store.get(key);
    // Refresh recency
    this._store.delete(key);
    this._store.set(key, value);
    return value;
  }

  /**
   * Store a value in the cache.
   * If the key already exists, its value is updated and it becomes
   * the most recently used entry. If the cache is full, the least
   * recently used entry is evicted.
   *
   * @param {*} key - The key under which to store the value.
   * @param {*} value - The value to store.
   * @returns {*} The stored value (allows chaining/inline use).
   */
  set(key, value) {
    // Refresh recency if key exists
    if (this._store.has(key)) {
      this._store.delete(key);
    } else if (this._store.size >= this._maxSize) {
      // Evict least recently used (first key in insertion order)
      const oldestKey = this._store.keys().next().value;
      this._store.delete(oldestKey);
    }
    this._store.set(key, value);
    return value;
  }

  /**
   * Check whether a key exists in the cache.
   * Does not affect recency order.
   *
   * @param {*} key - The key to check.
   * @returns {boolean} `true` if the key exists, otherwise `false`.
   */
  has(key) {
    return this._store.has(key);
  }

  /**
   * Remove a key from the cache.
   *
   * @param {*} key - The key to remove.
   * @returns {boolean} `true` if the key existed and was removed,
   *   `false` otherwise.
   */
  delete(key) {
    return this._store.delete(key);
  }
}

module.exports = Cache;
```

## Public API Summary

| Method | Signature | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `get` | `get(key) → *` | Returns the value for `key`, or `undefined` if absent. Marks the entry as recently used. |
| `set` | `set(key, value) → *` | Stores `value` under `key`. Evicts the least recently used entry if full. Returns the value. |
| `has` | `has(key) → boolean` | Returns `true` if `key` exists, without affecting recency. |
| `delete` | `delete(key) → boolean` | Removes `key`. Returns `true` if it existed, `false` otherwise. |

## Notes

- **Eviction policy:** LRU, implemented via `Map` insertion order (O(1) operations).
- **No TTL support:** entries persist until evicted or deleted. A time-based expiration could be added by storing `{ value, expiresAt }` tuples if needed.

